{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall pour upon his head and anoint.</b> Meaning, pouring upon his head is required and anointing in its own right is required, and likewise his sons, for the verse equates them together, as it is written ״וּמָשַׁחְתָּ אֹתָם״ (Exodus 28:41), and likewise in the portion of Pekudei (Exodus 40:15) it is written ״וּמָשַׁחְתָּ אֹתָם כַּאֲשֶׁר מָשַׁחְתָּ אֶת אֲבִיהֶם״, and so it is explicit in Torat Kohanim (in the portion of Tzav)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:21.448818500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}